# Playwright's output, for exactly the reason stated above: both are in
# .gitignore, Prettier 3 reads .gitignore by default, and this is the explicit
# copy so the exclusion does not depend on that default. `test-results/` holds
# traces, screenshots and videos from a failed run; `playwright-report/` is the
# HTML reporter's. Neither survives a green run, which is precisely why the
# exclusion has to be written down before anyone sees one — a red e2e run should
# not also turn `format:check` red.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The Python toolchain's virtualenv and caches, all five of which are also in
# .gitignore. Explicit copies, for the reason stated twice above: Prettier 3
# reads .gitignore by default, and this repository does not want an exclusion
# that depends on that default. `.venv/` is the one with teeth — it holds tens
# of thousands of installed files, some of them JSON and Markdown that Prettier
# would happily parse, and `prettier --check .` walking it is the difference
# between a fast gate and one people stop running.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The emitted OpenAPI document. Machine-generated by
# apps/api/src/scripts/emit-openapi.ts with `JSON.stringify(doc, null, 2)`, and
# diffed byte-for-byte against the committed copy. Prettier and JSON.stringify
# disagree permanently about the same file — printWidth: 100 collapses short
# arrays (`"required": ["status", "environment"]`) that JSON.stringify always
# expands — so leaving it formatted makes `format:check` fail on a freshly
# emitted document and the CI diff gate fail on a clean tree. A formatter is not
# the right owner for a generated artefact.
apps/api/openapi/
